<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">3 March in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 3 March, from 473 to 1991.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">473</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Glycerius proclaimed Western Roman Emperor</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Backed by the Burgundian general Gundobad, the court official Glycerius was proclaimed emperor at Ravenna. Deposed the next year, he was one of the short-lived final rulers of the Western Empire.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1585</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Teatro Olimpico opens in Vicenza</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Andrea Palladio's theatre opened with a performance of Sophocles's 'Oedipus Rex'. Its permanent painted street scenes survive, making it the oldest surviving enclosed theatre in the world.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1776</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Continental Marines land at Nassau in the Bahamas</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In their first amphibious operation, American marines and sailors captured two British forts on New Providence island, seizing cannon and military stores.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1845</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Florida becomes the 27th US state</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Florida, acquired from Spain in 1819, was admitted to the Union as a slave state. It seceded in 1861 and is now the third most populous state.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1848</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Lajos Kossuth demands constitutional reform for Hungary</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In the Hungarian Diet at Pressburg, Kossuth called for a responsible government and constitutional rule. His speech, made as revolution swept Europe, helped launch the Hungarian revolution of 1848.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungarian-diet">Hungarian Diet</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1878</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Treaty of San Stefano creates a 'Greater Bulgaria'</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Ending the Russo-Turkish War, the treaty created a large autonomous Bulgaria. The other great powers revised it at the Congress of Berlin that summer, leaving lasting Balkan grievances.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1918</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Soviet Russia signs the Treaty of Brest-Litovsk</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Bolsheviks made peace with the Central Powers, giving up Poland, the Baltic lands and Ukraine, with about a third of the old empire's population. Germany's defeat later voided the treaty.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-powers">Central Powers</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1923</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Time magazine publishes its first issue</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Founded by Henry Luce and Briton Hadden, Time summarised the week's news in a brisk, distinctive style. It became one of the most influential magazines in the world.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1991</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Rodney King's beating by Los Angeles police is filmed</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A bystander videotaped officers beating Rodney King after a car chase. The officers' acquittal in April 1992 sparked riots in Los Angeles in which more than 60 people died.</p></li></ol>
